export anchor CyberpunkNeonStyle:
    number: 299
    screen: CodeRepository
    name: Cyberpunk neon
    idea: A night city terminal in magenta and cyan neon on black, with cut corner panels, scanlines, a glitched headline and a hex grid of checks, loud in colour but strict about shape and contrast.
    base: dark
    palette:
        void: #07060b, the page and style sheet ground
        panel: #0f0c18, the terminal, shards and file rows
        panelRaised: #171226, raised fills
        ink: #f3eefe, text
        haze: #b3a9cc, labels, meta and line numbers
        grid: #3b2d5c, panel edges and tabs
        magenta: #ff3ddc, the primary button, headings, failing, removed lines and the header glow
        cyan: #2ef2ff, the current tab, passed, approved, added lines, links and focus
        volt: #ffe94d, changes requested, Private and the incoming comment
        magentaShade: #2a0c27, removed line ground
        cyanShade: #06232a, added line ground and passed hexes
    type:
        A wide sans, Eurostile, Microgramma, Bank Gothic, Segoe UI, at 800
        in caps for the title at 46px with a split magenta and cyan shadow
        offset 2px each way, and for section titles at 13px tracked 0.24em.
        Everything else is monospace, ui-monospace, Cascadia Mono, Menlo,
        at 14px and 1.5, labels 12px caps tracked 0.12em, the diff 13px.
    layout:
        A black ticker bar with a magenta rule and glow holds the app name
        as BRIGHTWORK//CODE, uplink stable and three outlined counters. A
        hero band follows with the repository in cyan caps, a volt Private
        tag, outlined tabs with the current one filled cyan and glowing,
        then the glitched title with the number in magenta, a broken neon
        underline in magenta and cyan, and the Open tag with the merge
        sentence. Faint scanlines cover the page. The body has a wide
        column and a 340px stack. The wide column holds the diff as a
        terminal with a prompt line, neon edges on added and removed lines
        and the comment as an incoming message box with a volt border and
        glow, then the three files as rows with a left edge. The stack
        holds three data shards, alternating cut corners. Checks shows
        11/12 and the twelve checks as hexagons, cyan with ticks, the
        failing one solid magenta with an octagon cross, then the failing
        line. Reviewers lists both verdicts. Metadata lists assignee,
        outlined labels, milestone and linked issue and a striped disabled
        merge button. Below 1000px the stack drops under the terminal.
    spacing: An 8px unit. 24px page gutters, 20px column gap, 16px shard padding.
    density: Medium. A large headline band, then a wide terminal beside a stack of shards.
    corners: Cut corners, 18px clipped on alternate shards, a 9px notch on the primary button, hexagon check cells.
    borders: 1px violet grid lines, 2px neon edges on diff lines and file rows, a magenta rule under the ticker.
    shadows: Neon glows only, magenta under the ticker and primary button, cyan on the current tab and focus, volt on the comment.
    icons:
        2px line icons. A tick for passed and an octagon cross for failing
        inside hexes, a ringed tick for approved, a triangle for changes,
        each with a caps word.
    focus: A 2px cyan outline offset 3px with a cyan glow.
    tone: Terminal slang kept readable, such as uplink stable, incoming and Merge locked.
